<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabula Rapinensis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Rapino bronze</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tabula Rapinensis is a small bronze tablet found at Rapino in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, inscribed in the Italic dialect of the Marrucini in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alphabet, probably in the 3rd century BCE. It records a sacred regulation of the community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chieti">Teate</a>, apparently about the cult of Jupiter and of a goddess, and is the main surviving text in the Marrucinian dialect.</p></div>
